pular","narrativeScore":0,"accessibilityScore":0.533,"scholarlyScore":0.098,"traits":[{"id":"popular","score":0.772,"confidence":"high","evidence":["catalog text contains \"bestseller\"","catalog text contains \"new york times bestseller\"","trade publisher signal: Random House Trade Paperbacks / Penguin Random House","major-award recognition"]},{"id":"accessible","score":0.68,"confidence":"medium","evidence":["catalog text contains \"bestseller\"","catalog text contains \"new york times bestseller\"","trade publisher signal: Random House Trade Paperbacks / Penguin Random House"]},{"id":"argument_driven","score":0.2,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"argues\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"The principal threat to American democracy came from within, because the Trump presidency weakened institutions and compromised the Republican Party, making the peril likely to last for years and requiring vigilance against authoritarianism.","confidence":0.74},"academicOrientation":{"score":35,"confidence":0.55},"profileConfidence":0.78,"model":"gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"b2278c1ffccbbdb4da9e49f17e2c6dfcfb99dc8c442cfbaa571e03e3eebf5257","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"primarySubject":"Politics & Government","secondarySubjects":["American History","Memoir & Autobiography"],"confidence":"high","rationale":"The book primarily discusses the political landscape of America during Donald Trump's presidency, while also incorporating personal experiences from Schiff's political career.","method":"llm","model":"gpt-4o-mini","reviewStatus":"generated","inputHash":"b5757800d5c82f8a23ecb3b007d60a0f0d3b9df6cbe370a33cf6d258bc5bacc8","summary":"\"From the congressman who led the first impeachment of Donald J. Trump, the vital inside account of American democracy in its darkest hour, and a warning that the forces of autocracy unleashed by Trump remain as potent as ever. In the years leading up to the election of Donald Trump, Congressman Adam Schiff had already been sounding the alarm over the resurgence of autocracy around the world, and the threat this posed to the United States. But as he led the probe into Donald Trump's Russia and Ukraine-related abuses of presidential power, Schiff came to the terrible conclusion that the principal threat to American democracy now came from within. In Midnight in Washington, Schiff argues that the Trump presidency has so weakened our institutions and compromised the Republican Party that the peril will last for years, requiring unprecedented vigilance against the growing and dangerous appeal of authoritarianism. The congressman chronicles step by step just how our democracy was put at such risk, and traces his own path to meeting the crisis--from serious prosecutor, to congressman with an expertise in national security and a reputation for bipartisanship, to liberal lightning rod, scourge of the right, and archenemy of a president.","subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"nyt:combined-print-and-e-book-nonfiction=2021-10-31","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-midnight-in-washington-how-we-almost-lost-our-democracy-and-still-could-adam-schiff"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"New York Times bestseller","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-midnight-in-washington-how-we-almost-lost-our-democracy-and-still-could-adam-schiff"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Influence","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-midnight-in-washington-how-we-almost-lost-our-democracy-and-still-could-adam-schiff"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Politics and government","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-midnight-in-washington-how-we-almost-lost-our-democracy-and-still-could-adam-schiff"